Use a buffer-backed TGSI constant slot for the graphics compositor.

Convert RGB to NV12 with the RGB-to-YUV matrix. Sample the visible rectangle in pixel coordinates before normalizing against the backing texture so VirGL dma-buf padding stays outside the visible picture.

